<title>USA: FSA qualifies seven muni issues for bond insurance.</title>
<headline>FSA qualifies seven muni issues for bond insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financial Security Assurance said on Wednesday that it qualified for insurance the following seven  municipal bond issues scheduled for competitive sale today :</p>
<p>--Des Moines, Iowa, $21.68 million water revenues.</p>
<p>--Lafourche School District, La., $10 million General Obligations (GOs).</p>
<p>--Holbrook, Mass., GOs $4.8 million.</p>
<p>--Geneva, N.Y., $1.18 million public improvement bonds.</p>
<p>--Sprinville, N.Y., $1.666 million various purpose bonds.</p>
<p>--Wilson School District, Pa., $34 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Knoxville, Tenn., GOs, $23.34 million public improvement.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
